3. Object-Oriented Programming (OOP)
Java is fundamentally object-oriented. This example demonstrates a simple object class and its instantiation. 
java

// Class blueprint definition
class Car {
    String brand;
    int year;

    // Constructor to initialize attributes
    public Car(String brand, int year) {
        this.brand = brand;
        this.year = year;
    }

    // Object behavior method
    public void displayDetails() {
        System.out.println("Car Brand: " + brand + ", Year: " + year);
    }
}

// Main execution class
public class OOPExample {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        // Instantiating a new Car object
        Car myCar = new Car("Toyota", 2025);
        
        // Calling a method on the object
        myCar.displayDetails();
    }
}

